recorded 2026-11-12 8.1.17 neutralized
The T034 spike (research.md "8.1 webservice spike (T034)") on a non-production 8.1.17 server without a cluster: D-2 steps 1-5 ok, getNode a non-empty node name, clusterDownload of webservice.log without exception, nothing on stderr, exit 0. The throwaway program printed its steps, not helper frames, so ok.frames is written in the helper protocol (D-4, D-5) with the fixed nonce, node name node1 (the recorded name is replaced) and the byte count of ok.log; its two log4j lines are taken over from fixtures/queue-entry/v8_1/garbage_frames.frames, not from T034.
Neutralized as in research D-21: the recorded log (about 22.4 million bytes of plain ASCII) is replaced by a fictitious log of the same shape. Mirrors the recording: "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss,SSS <id> [WebService ...]" entries continued by HTTP header blocks and SOAP bodies; lowercase request headers (host, content-type, soapaction, accept-encoding, x-forwarded-for, traceparent, x-amzn-trace-id); response headers Set-Cookie, Date, Content-Type, Server, X-Frame-Options, Cache-Control; a wsse:UsernameToken without a wsse:Password child. Invented: all values (acme services, inubit.example.test, partner.example.test, 192.0.2.x, trace ids, cookies), the entry ids, content-length, the request and status lines and the text after "[WebService". Fictitious masking probes, as the recording has no Authorization header and no password element: the outgoing Call and Call response entries with one Authorization: Basic header and the second wsse:UsernameToken with one wsse:Password element.
